Scope build SSH identities to configured keys

Use a fresh agent for builds that enable SSH forwarding when
sshAgent.keys is explicit, so only the configured identities are
exposed. Preserve existing forwarding when sshAgent is unset or ambient,
and avoid creating a build agent when SSH forwarding is disabled.

Point build SSH sources at the temporary socket while preserving the
ambient agent for remote Docker authentication. Reuse pod agent startup
and cleanup so key paths and errors stay consistent across Dockerfile,
preparation, and Compose builds.

Cover key isolation, fresh agents, cleanup, absent and empty key lists,
and unchanged ambient forwarding with integration tests.
